so the lore and elden ring is probably  one of the most complicated pieces of  storytelling i've ever tried to  understand one day i'll believe  something about the overall theme and  the objective of the game and the next  day i'll believe something completely  different based on some item description  i read off of some random flower  everything seems to connect while at the  same time discrediting everything else  i've spent the better part of this year  completely dedicated to learning and  understanding the world of elden ring  the moment i think i'm getting somewhere  is also the moment where i'm the most  confused it's like the game is designed  to be confusing and that's likely  because it was designed this way trying  to connect all of the dots when it comes  to elden ring lore is next to impossible  the best way for all of us to get  concrete evidence about what certain  things mean and connect to are the item  descriptions we can read on almost every  item in the game the only reason i say  concrete evidence is because it's plain  as day written down by the developers to  tell us what something is what it does  and what it means the rest of the  evidence we can gather from the game on  the lore isn't concrete in the slightest  dialogue is important in helping us  understand the intentions of other  characters we meet in the game but i  think it's important to note that even  npcs in the game can be wrong all the  characters have their own beliefs  perspectives and intentions the path one  character has journeyed on by the time  we meet and talk to them can be  drastically different from another  character that goes without saying but  it's not like we haven't been  manipulated into thinking one thing  based on what one character says and we  only learned later on that they were  just trying to swindle us and trick us  into just doing what they wanted so i  guess i shouldn't say that some  characters are wrong they're just as  confused as we are or they just believe  something different from us because  they've had a different experience in  the lands between than we have and that  just goes to show why there seems to be  such a divide in the community about the  lore of elden ring it's because we've  all had different experiences while  playing the game we're all going to have  different interpretations of what  something means what a character says  and what the environment is trying to  tell us it's all going to be different  for each person because we're all  different people with our own thoughts  beliefs aspirations doubts achievements  guidance and ultimately experiences and  that's the entire point of the game for  every player to have their own unique  experiences while playing the game and  sure there's guiding lights that tell us  where to go and weird characters telling  us what to do but how many of us  actually followed that line to a t and  listened to the first character we met  well apparently a lot of people did and  got tilted from it when it led us  straight to one of the hardest opening  bosses in all of video game history some  people will see this as annoying get  absolutely destroyed by market and quit  the game because they think it's too  hard they're too bad at the game and  they'll never be able to make it past  this obstacle then there's the other  type of person who won't follow that  light whatsoever and go explore every  area of the map find resources to  upgrade their weapons defeat every enemy  in a certain area thoroughly search  every dungeon in hidden area and they  won't even know margate exists until  about 40 hours into their first  playthrough this is just an example of  what i'm talking about we are all going  to have different experiences which is  why we're all going to have different  interpretations of the lore presented to  us in a completely non-linear way  because the game is completely open and  non-linear itself this non-linear  storytelling is not bad storytelling  it's completely by design it's meant to  match the experience of the game itself  and it's meant to be up to  interpretation of the player in their  own personal journey through the game  and then coming up with theories made by  everyone in the community when i make my  lore videos i receive a ton of comments  that just say no this is completely  wrong followed by paragraphs of  describing their own theory on that  subject and i think saying a theory in  elden ring could be straight up wrong is  like someone telling you your taste in  coffee is wrong just because i like a  little cream and sugar with my coffee  doesn't mean you drinking straight black  decaf is wrong i could think you're  weird for doing and thinking that and  tell you my own preference but you  aren't wrong for thinking that way i  think most people who think certain  theories can be wrong are likely players  who are mostly new to the souls games  they just don't understand that the  creators of these games purposely tell  stories like this i think zoli the witch  said it perfectly in a recent tweet  where she said something to always keep  in mind with lore discussion and from  software is that miyazaki isn't  interested in correct lore from  deliberately denies you information so  you can't really be certain what  miyazaki wants is for you to guess to  engage in media speculation and this is  exactly what i'm trying to say we aren't  meant to know the full story and we  aren't meant to know definitive  information on anything it's all up to  interpretation it's all up to your own  imagination from software does this  because they respect you as a player and  a person they believe that you're smart  enough to figure it out on your own and  like i said before this matches the  gameplay perfectly they don't tell you  how to do everything in the game from  the start because they want you to  figure it out and experience it on your  own they don't tell you what to do  because they want you to find your own  path they don't give you a quest log on  where to find the next npc location  because it makes it that much more  special when you find it on your own  does it make the experience harder  absolutely it does but if everything was  easy then it wouldn't be really worth  doing most games nowadays think the  players have absolutely no brain of  their own and they have to be handheld  through every single thing in the game  some of these games don't even let you  play the real game until you complete a  mundane tutorial where elden ring just  lets you walk right past it if that's  what you want to do from software gives  you the freedom to do anything that you  want to do and i appreciate their game  so much more because of this the best  way that i could put all of this is that  the story of elden ring is like a  painting when you look at a painting  you're going to have your own  interpretation of what that painting  means and what it's trying to show you  one person may think something totally  different from another about that  painting but it doesn't mean any  interpretation is wrong it's simply just  different is there anything wrong with  that of course there isn't it's a  beautiful thing to see others speculate  in different ways about something else  but for whatever reason some people just  don't like it when other people think  differently from them some of my best  friends and i think differently about  politics for example but it doesn't mean  that i don't still love them and love  being around them as a friend we just  think differently about certain things  it also doesn't mean that they're wrong  and i'm right or the other way around it  just means we think differently and  there's nothing wrong with that when it  comes to elden rings lore it's the same  way i may disagree about allure theory  but i'd never tell them that they're  just straight up wrong because i have no  idea if they're right or wrong because  none of us know it's just what they  think and what i think we can debate  speculate and make our own theories but  none of us are right or wrong we are  simply doing exactly what the game was  designed for us to do we are meant to  come up with our own interpretations  based on our own experiences it is so  much fun to watch videos on theories  that i may completely disagree with  because i love watching people speculate  and create theories that's a huge part  of the fun and it becomes not as fun  when people just argue and complain  about a theory that none of us really  know any definitive information on it  truly is amazing to see elden ring hit  the mainstream audience and it's brought  a ton of new players into the game and i  couldn't be happier about that and  obviously that's going to bring in some  players who just do not understand the  lore of all the souls games i just  wanted to talk about this topic as it's  something i feel pretty strongly about  so thank you guys for watching and thank  you all so much for 40 000 subscribers  it means the world to me so just know i  appreciate every single one of you the  next video will definitely be another  lore video on either malacath or an  updated theory on gideon off near so let  me know what you want to see next have a  great rest of your day and i'll see you  all in the next video take care  [Music]  you
 

